course: dictionary
lesson: 4728
title: Horde: a crowd, or a warrior group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A horde is a very large crowd, often noisy or out of control. You can find its meaning from the words around it. In «hordes of shoppers», the word hordes tells you there were far more people than usual.
explain: In history, a horde means a large group of nomadic warriors, people who moved from place to place. Ask yourself whether the story is about a crowd of people or about an army on horseback. The words around the word give the clue.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A horde of zombies attacks the village» still makes sense with «a huge, noisy crowd of zombies», so the meaning fits. Watch for the phrases «hordes of» and «a horde of».
fact: A horde is a very large crowd, often noisy or out of control.
fact: In history, a horde was a large group of nomadic warriors, such as the Mongol horde.
fact: «Hordes of» means lots of, in big crowds.
fact: Nomadic means moving from place to place rather than living in one town.
fact: The Golden Horde was one of the separate Mongol khanates, and it ruled over Moscow in 1337.
exercise: «Hordes of shoppers crowded into the sale.» What does hordes mean here? | *A very large, busy crowd | A small, quiet group of friends | A long, empty road | A type of shop
exercise: Ella reads about the Mongol horde riding across Asia on horseback. What is a horde in history? | *A large group of nomadic warriors | A quiet village of farmers | A castle with high walls | A kind of Mongol horse
exercise: «A horde of kids ran into the park.» What does a horde of tell you? | A very small group | Nothing at all | Just one child | *A big, busy crowd
test:
«The stadium was filled with a horde of fans.» Horde is closest in meaning to which word? | Silence | Calm | *Crowd | Hush
«Moscow was a small principality under the overlordship of the Golden Horde in 1337.» What is the Golden Horde? | *A large Mongol group of warriors and their state | A kind of tourist trip | A shop in Moscow | A small village ruled by a farmer
exam:
In «a horde of zombies attacks the village», what does horde mean? | A tiny group of three | A friendly family | *A very large, often out of control crowd | A type of village
